course: dictionary
lesson: 15192
title: Sedate: calm and slow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sedate has two meanings, and the sentence tells you which one. Most often it is an adjective that describes someone or something as calm, slow and quiet, without excitement. «The sedate old tortoise walked slowly across the lawn.» Nothing about the tortoise is rushed or wild, so sedate means calm and slow.
explain: Sedate can also be a verb. When a vet or doctor sedates an animal or a person, they give them medicine that makes them calm or sleepy. «The vet had to sedate the frightened dog before the operation.» The dog was given medicine so it could be treated safely.
explain: To choose the right meaning, look at the clues around the word. Is the sentence describing something as calm and slow, or is someone giving medicine? Then swap in your meaning. «They walked at a calm, slow pace along the river» still makes sense, so the first meaning fits.
fact: Sedate (adjective) means calm, slow and quiet, without excitement.
fact: A sedate pace is a slow, calm speed.
fact: A sedate life is calm and quiet, with little excitement.
fact: Sedate (verb) means to give a person or animal medicine that makes them calm or sleepy.
fact: Vets sedate animals so they can be treated safely, and doctors may sedate patients before an operation.
exercise: «The sedate old tortoise walked slowly across the lawn.» What does sedate mean here? | *Calm and slow | Bright and shiny | Lost and hungry | Fast and noisy
exercise: «The vet had to sedate the frightened dog before the operation.» What does sedate mean here? | To wash the dog | To run away from | To play with | *To give medicine that makes the dog calm or sleepy
exercise: In «They walked at a sedate pace along the quiet river», find and copy the word that describes the pace. | along | walked | *sedate | river
test: «The sedate museum visitors moved slowly from room to room.» What does sedate suggest? | Lost | Loud and excited | Hungry | *Calm and quiet
test: «Doctors may sedate a patient before a big operation.» Here sedate means what? | *To give medicine that makes the patient calm or sleepy | To cook a meal | To run a race | To paint the room
exam: Ella says «sedate» is just another word for fast. Why is she wrong? | Sedate means fast and exciting | Sedate is a type of food | Sedate means the same as fast | *Sedate means calm and slow, the opposite of fast
